A download can take a while, and the user may import a PDF for the same
key meanwhile, most likely because this very download looked hopeless.
A file the user fetched by hand must never be replaced by a later
automatic one, so the download is put in place under the lock that
import and clear share (\cref{sec:pdf-cache-imports}), after a last look
at the key: if it now holds an import (a file its record matches), the
import stays and the downloaded copy is discarded.
The lock is held for that look and the rename only, never during the
transfer, which could otherwise keep an import waiting for minutes.
An import that starts after the rename finds the download in place and
needs [[--replace]], as for any download.

