\subsection{Downloading by DOI}
\label{sec:pdf-download-doi}

A DOI has several candidate URLs (\cref{sec:doi-resolution}) and any of
them can disappoint: the link is dead, or it answers with HTML because
we are not on a network the publisher admits.
[[download_pdf]] already turns each of these into a
[[PDFDownloadError]], so falling through is a loop around it.
We keep the reasons, since when every candidate fails the user is best
served by seeing each source's failure, not only the last; the
[[skip]] parameter lets a caller exclude a URL it has tried already.
Before any of that, a PDF the user imported for this DOI
(\cref{sec:pdf-import}) is used as it is: it is the copy the candidates
failed to deliver, or the user would not have imported it, and finding
it costs no request.

<<pdf download functions>>=
def download_doi_pdf(
    doi: str,
    progress_callback: Callable[[str], None] | None = None,
    skip: tuple[str, ...] = (),
    written: str | None = None,
) -> Path:
    """
    Download the PDF for a DOI, trying each candidate URL in turn.

    `written` is the DOI as a doi.org URL wrote it, before decoding, so
    that a PDF imported under that older key is found.

    Raises:
        PDFDownloadError: If no source names a PDF, or none delivers;
            the message lists every attempt.
    """
    for imported in doi_pdf_paths(doi, written):
        if usable_cached_pdf(imported):
            if progress_callback:
                progress_callback(f"Using imported PDF: {imported}")
            return imported
    failures = []
    for source, url in doi_pdf_candidates(doi, progress_callback):
        if url in skip:
            continue
        try:
            return download_pdf(url, progress_callback)
        except PDFDownloadError as e:
            reason = str(e).splitlines()[0]
            logger.info("PDF via %s failed for %s: %s", source, doi, reason)
            failures.append(f"{source}: {reason} ({url})")
    if not failures:
        raise PDFDownloadError(
            f"Could not find open access PDF for DOI: {doi}\n"
            f"The paper may not be available as open access."
        )
    raise PDFDownloadError(
        f"No source delivered a PDF for DOI: {doi}\n"
        + "\n".join(failures)
    )
@

\subsection{High-level PDF access}

For convenience, we provide a function that accepts a Paper object, a DOI,
or a URL string, making it easy to use from both programmatic code and
the CLI/TUI.
A paper's own [[pdf_url]] is one more candidate, tried first because a
provider named it for this very record; if it fails and the paper has a
DOI, the DOI's candidates follow.

A copy already on disk comes before any request, though: a PDF
imported for the paper's DOI (\cref{sec:pdf-import}), else the cached
download of the [[pdf_url]].
Without that, a paper whose [[pdf_url]] answers with a login page would
make the full-text classification ask the publisher again on every
run, and fail, before it reached the PDF the user imported by DOI.
The import comes first because the user made it on purpose, most likely
because the download of that very [[pdf_url]] failed: a copy the
download left behind is the one the user meant to replace.
A DOI that is not a non-empty string (a test double's attribute, a
list from a malformed record) is no DOI, rather than a crash in the
key function.

<<pdf download functions>>=
def get_pdf(
    source: Any,
    progress_callback: Callable[[str], None] | None = None,
) -> Path:
    """
    Get a PDF, downloading if necessary.
    
    This is the main entry point for PDF access. It accepts:
    - A Paper object (using its pdf_url or doi attributes)
    - A DOI string (resolved via Unpaywall/Semantic Scholar)
    - A direct URL string
    
    Args:
        source: A Paper object, DOI string, or URL string.
        progress_callback: Optional callback for status messages.
    
    Returns:
        Path to the cached PDF file.
    
    Raises:
        PDFDownloadError: If download fails or no PDF available.
    """
    if isinstance(source, str):
        doi = extract_doi(source)
        if doi:
            logger.debug("Source is a DOI: %s", doi)
            if progress_callback:
                progress_callback(f"Resolving DOI: {doi}")
            return download_doi_pdf(
                doi, progress_callback, written=doi_url_path(source)
            )
        logger.debug("Source is a URL: %s", source)
        return download_pdf(source, progress_callback)

    paper_title = getattr(source, "title", "Unknown")
    logger.debug("Getting PDF for paper: %s", paper_title)
    url = getattr(source, "pdf_url", None)
    doi = getattr(source, "doi", None)
    if not (isinstance(doi, str) and doi.strip()):
        doi = None
    if not url and not doi:
        logger.warning("Paper has no PDF URL or DOI: %s", paper_title)
        raise PDFDownloadError(
            f"Paper has no PDF URL or DOI: {paper_title}"
        )
    <<use a copy on disk before any request>>
    first_failure = None
    if url:
        try:
            return download_pdf(url, progress_callback)
        except PDFDownloadError as e:
            if not doi:
                raise
            first_failure = str(e).splitlines()[0]
            logger.info("pdf_url failed for %s; trying its DOI", paper_title)
    if progress_callback:
        progress_callback(f"Resolving DOI: {doi}")
    try:
        return download_doi_pdf(
            doi, progress_callback, skip=(url,) if url else ()
        )
    except PDFDownloadError as e:
        if first_failure is None:
            raise
        raise PDFDownloadError(
            f"{e}\nThe paper's own link: {first_failure} ({url})"
        ) from e
@

