A URL that is a DOI's resolver URL is taken as that DOI, because that
is how [[get_pdf]] reads it: [[pdf quote https://doi.org/...]] looks up
the DOI, so an import under that URL's own key would never be found.
The record keeps the URL as given beside the DOI it named.
A DOI that does not have the form of one, once normalised, is refused
rather than imported under a key nothing will look up.
A resolver URL whose DOI was keyed as written before it was decoded
([[doi_pdf_paths]], \cref{sec:pdf-import-key}) goes to that old key when
a copy is there and none under the decoded key, so that the comparison
below judges the existing copy and the import never leaves a second
one.

