Let's verify that an import made before resolver URLs were decoded is
still found and still counts as the paper's one copy.
The old import is made as the code before the change made it: its key
is the resolver URL with the DOI as the URL wrote it, which an import
by that spelling of the DOI produces exactly.
The lookups must find it without a request ([[requests.get]] fails the
test if called), and importing the same file again by the URL must
answer \enquote{unchanged}, another file must need [[--replace]], and
the cache must hold one PDF throughout.

